If you're using the .DSW, the makefile has no effect.

Since you want the console version, I think it's safe to say you're comfortable
with a command line.  To use the makefile:

* Open a command shell
* Go to the top of your NetHack tree
* Set up the environment variables with something like
  C:\Program Files\Microsoft Visual Studio\Visual C++ 6\bin\vcvars32.bat
  I'm not sure of the directory, so you might want to do
  dir /s C:\Program Files\Microsoft Visual Studio\vcvars32.bat
  to make sure you have the right directory.
* Edit your make file for the console version (you did it correctly) and
  type nmake to build.

There is a setting in the .DSW but I can never remember exactly how to find it,
and I don't have that specific version of VC++ available.



